From: Akisaira <akisaira@outlook.com>
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: sc8280xp-huawei-gaokun3: keep VCC_WLAN_3R9
 on

pcie4 uses this rail as its vddpe-3v3, and qcom_pcie_deinit_2_7_0()
disables that supply whenever the link goes down. skip_pwrctrl_off does
not cover it: it only keeps the wlan power sequencer target of wifi@0.
So a link that enters L2 with WoWLAN armed loses the rail while the
firmware keeps running and the chip stays associated.

The Windows PEP tables configure PMR735A GPIO1 in the D0 list of PCI6 and
have no step for it in D3, so Windows sleeps with the rail on. Do the same
with regulator-always-on. The driver's enable and disable calls stay
balanced and have no effect on the rail.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
Origin: local
Upstream-Status: Pending
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sc8280xp-huawei-gaokun3.dts | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sc8280xp-huawei-gaokun3.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sc8280xp-huawei-gaokun3.dts
index e60582c91..691cbc7f2 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sc8280xp-huawei-gaokun3.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sc8280xp-huawei-gaokun3.dts
@@ -203,6 +203,11 @@ vreg_wlan: regulator-wlan {
 		pinctrl-0 = <&hastings_reg_en>;
 		pinctrl-names = "default";
 
+		/*
+		 * pcie4 disables its vddpe-3v3 whenever the link goes down, and
+		 * the firmware keeps running in L2 with WoWLAN armed.
+		 */
+		regulator-always-on;
 		regulator-boot-on;
 	};
 
